<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
	<Task>
		<Title>Deploy YARA-X Signatures - Universal</Title>
		<Description><![CDATA[<P>Deploys the YARA rule files used by the &quot;Scan with YARA-X Signatures&quot; tasks into the YARA engine signatures directory, <CODE>__BESData/__Global/__MitigationToolkit/yara/signatures</CODE>, and creates the rest of the engine layout (<CODE>bin</CODE>, <CODE>results</CODE>, <CODE>work</CODE>).</P><P>Four rule files are written. Three are copies of <A href="https://github.com/jgstew/tools/tree/master/YARA">jgstew/tools YARA</A> <CODE>php/php_detect.yar</CODE>, <CODE>node/node_detect.yar</CODE> and <CODE>apache/apache_detect.yar</CODE>; <CODE>java_detect.yar</CODE> reports the version and distribution vendor of a JRE or JDK. The scan task passes the whole signatures directory to <CODE>yr scan</CODE>, which walks it for <CODE>.yar</CODE> and <CODE>.yara</CODE> files, so every signature in it is included. Add your own rule files there and they are picked up by the next scan; rule identifiers have to be unique across the directory.</P><P>Run this task before the scan tasks. The scan tasks are not relevant until at least one signature file is present. The version of the deployed set is recorded in <CODE>__MitigationToolkit/yara/signatures.version</CODE>, and this task becomes relevant again whenever that file does not match the version it ships (2026-11-17.5).</P>]]></Description>
		<Relevance><![CDATA[not in proxy agent context]]></Relevance>
		<Relevance><![CDATA[not exists files whose(name of it = "signatures.version" and exists lines whose(it = "2026-11-17.5") of it) of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client]]></Relevance>
		<Category></Category>
		<Source>Internal</Source>
		<SourceID>jgstew</SourceID>
		<SourceReleaseDate>2026-11-17</SourceReleaseDate>
		<SourceSeverity></SourceSeverity>
		<CVENames></CVENames>
		<SANSID></SANSID>
		<MIMEField>
			<Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
			<Value>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</Value>
		</MIMEField>
		<Domain>BESC</Domain>
		<DefaultAction ID="Action1">
			<Description>
				<PreLink>Click </PreLink>
				<Link>here</Link>
				<PostLink> to deploy the YARA-X signatures.</PostLink>
			</Description>
			<ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell"><![CDATA[
// Deploy the YARA rule files into the YARA engine signatures directory.
// Rule text is copied from YARA/php/php_detect.yar, YARA/node/node_detect.yar
// and YARA/apache/apache_detect.yar in https://github.com/jgstew/tools by
// YARA/sync_rules.py - edit them there, not here.

// The scan engine layout, under the client data folder (the __BESData folder).
// One path separator per platform: relevance does not translate them.
parameter "sep" = "{if (windows of operating system) then "\" else "/"}"
parameter "global_folder" = "{pathname of data folders of client}{parameter "sep"}__Global"
parameter "toolkit_root" = "{parameter "global_folder"}{parameter "sep"}__MitigationToolkit"
parameter "engine_folder" = "{parameter "toolkit_root"}{parameter "sep"}yara"
parameter "signatures_folder" = "{parameter "engine_folder"}{parameter "sep"}signatures"

// folder create is not recursive, so each level is created in turn. Each one is
// guarded: __Global normally exists already, and the task reruns on a version change.
if {not exists folders "__Global" of data folders of client}
	folder create "{parameter "global_folder"}"
endif
if {not exists folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client}
	folder create "{parameter "toolkit_root"}"
endif
if {not exists folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client}
	folder create "{parameter "engine_folder"}"
endif
if {not exists folders "signatures" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client}
	folder create "{parameter "signatures_folder"}"
endif
// bin holds yr.exe / yr, results holds the scan output, work is the scan scratch
// area. The scan task needs all three; creating them here keeps the layout in one place.
if {not exists folders "bin" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client}
	folder create "{parameter "engine_folder"}{parameter "sep"}bin"
endif
if {not exists folders "results" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client}
	folder create "{parameter "engine_folder"}{parameter "sep"}results"
endif
if {not exists folders "work" of folders "yara" of folders "__MitigationToolkit" of folders "__Global" of data folders of client}
	folder create "{parameter "engine_folder"}{parameter "sep"}work"
endif

// The version marker is written last, and lives beside the signatures folder
// rather than in it: yr scan walks the signatures folder for rule files.
// Every left curly brace below is doubled, BigFix's escape for relevance substitution.

// php_detect.yar
delete __createfile
createfile until _END_OF_RULE_
/*
  PHP install detection + version, all OSes (Linux ELF, Windows PE, macOS Mach-O).

  Deliberately broad: PHP_Binary_Broad flags anything that looks PHP-related so
  nothing is missed; the other rules carry the exact version string. Run with
  `yara -s` (or `yr scan -s`) to print the matched version text.

  Rules:
    PHP_Runtime_Version     - PHP core runtime; $ver holds the exact version,
                              incl. distro suffix (e.g. 8.1.2-1ubuntu2.27)
    PHP_Windows_VersionInfo - any PE whose version resource says ProductName=PHP
                              (php.exe, php-cgi.exe, php8ts.dll, ext\php_*.dll);
                              $pv holds ProductVersion
    PHP_Binary_Broad        - catch-all: any executable with any PHP marker

  No modules are imported so the rules also work in embedded YARA engines
  (osquery, EDRs) that are built without the pe/elf/macho modules.

  See README.md for tested samples and the API number -> branch table.
*/

// Condition copied from is_executable.yar by sync_rules.py - edit it there
private rule PHP_Detect_IsExecutable
{{
  condition:
    // ELF executable (2) or shared object (3, also PIE executables); e_type is
    // in the byte order given by EI_DATA (1 = little, 2 = big endian)
    (uint32(0) == 0x464C457F and
      ((uint8(5) == 1 and (uint16(16) == 2 or uint16(16) == 3)) or
       (uint8(5) == 2 and (uint16be(16) == 2 or uint16be(16) == 3))))
    // PE: MZ header whose e_lfanew (0x3C) points at "PE\0\0"
    or (uint16(0) == 0x5A4D and uint32(uint32(0x3C)) == 0x00004550)
    // Mach-O 32/64 execute (2), dylib (6) or bundle (8, e.g. PHP extensions)
    or ((uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
        (uint32(12) == 2 or uint32(12) == 6 or uint32(12) == 8))
    // same, byte-swapped (big-endian) Mach-O
    or ((uint32(0) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(0) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
        (uint32be(12) == 2 or uint32be(12) == 6 or uint32be(12) == 8))
    // Mach-O universal (CAFEBABE) with 1-19 architectures whose first slice
    // passes the thin Mach-O check above, so universal static libraries (.a),
    // object files and dSYMs are rejected. Java .class files also start with
    // CAFEBABE, but bytes 4-7 hold their class version (major >= 45), not an
    // architecture count. The header is big-endian; the first slice's offset
    // is at 16 (fat_arch.offset).
    or (uint32(0) == 0xBEBAFECA and uint32be(4) > 0 and uint32be(4) < 20 and
        (((uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
          (uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 2 or uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 8)) or
         ((uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
          (uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 2 or uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 8))))
    // same for the rare 64-bit universal header (CAFEBABF): fat_arch_64.offset
    // is 8 bytes at 16; slices sit well below 4 GB, so its low half (20) is used
    or (uint32(0) == 0xBFBAFECA and uint32be(4) > 0 and uint32be(4) < 20 and
        (((uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
          (uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 2 or uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 8)) or
         ((uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
          (uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 2 or uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 8))))
}

rule PHP_Runtime_Version
{{
  meta:
    description = "PHP core runtime (CLI/CGI/FPM/mod_php/libphp/php*ts.dll/php8.dll/embedded); $ver = exact version"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // Compile-time literal "X-Powered-By: PHP/" PHP_VERSION in main/SAPI.c.
    // Present regardless of expose_php. Suffix covers distro builds (8.1.2-1ubuntu2.27)
    // and pre-releases (8.5.0RC1).
    $ver = /X-Powered-By: PHP\/[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}/
  condition:
    PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and $ver
}

rule PHP_Windows_VersionInfo
{{
  meta:
    description = "Windows PE with PHP version resource; $pv = ProductVersion (exact version)"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // UTF-16LE "ProductName" <NUL + 0-2 bytes alignment pad> "PHP\0"
    $pname = {{ 50 00 72 00 6F 00 64 00 75 00 63 00 74 00 4E 00 61 00 6D 00 65 00 [2-4] 50 00 48 00 50 00 00 00 }
    $pv = /ProductVersion\x00[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.\-]{{0,20}/ wide
  condition:
    // A real PE (MZ + PE signature). #pv >= 0 is always true: $pv is only
    // there so -s prints the version
    uint16(0) == 0x5A4D and PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and $pname and #pv >= 0
}

rule PHP_Binary_Broad
{{
  meta:
    description = "Broad catch-all: executable containing any PHP runtime/extension marker"
    confidence = "medium"
  strings:
    $xpb    = "X-Powered-By: PHP/"
    $zend   = "Zend Engine v"
    // ZEND_MODULE_BUILD_ID, e.g. API20220829,NTS / API20250925,TS - also in extensions
    $api    = /API20[0-9]{{6},N?TS/
    $pname  = {{ 50 00 72 00 6F 00 64 00 75 00 63 00 74 00 4E 00 61 00 6D 00 65 00 [2-4] 50 00 48 00 50 00 00 00 }
    $grp    = "The PHP Group" ascii wide
    $ini    = "php.ini"
    $fmt    = "PHP %s (%s)"
  condition:
    PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and
    (
      $xpb or $zend or $api or $pname
      or ($grp and ($ini or $fmt))
    )
}
_END_OF_RULE_
delete "{parameter "signatures_folder"}{parameter "sep"}php_detect.yar"
move __createfile "{parameter "signatures_folder"}{parameter "sep"}php_detect.yar"

// node_detect.yar
delete __createfile
createfile until _END_OF_RULE_
/*
  Node.js install detection + version, all OSes (Linux ELF, Windows PE, macOS Mach-O).

  Finds standalone node / node.exe, distro libnode, and Node embedded in other
  software (Electron, single-executable applications, vercel/pkg, apps that
  bundle libnode). Deliberately broad: Node_Binary_Broad flags anything that
  looks Node-related so nothing is missed; the other rules carry the exact
  version string. Run with `yara -s` (or `yr scan -s`) to print the matched
  version text.

  Rules:
    Node_Runtime_Version  - Node runtime or a runtime embedding Node; $ver holds
                            the exact version (node.js/v22.23.4), or for pkg
                            builds with no inspector $rel (the release URL)
    Node_Electron_Version - Electron framework; $electron holds Electron's
                            version, $ver the embedded Node version (none
                            in very old Electron, around 2.x)
    Node_Binary_Broad     - catch-all: any executable with any Node marker,
                            incl. native addons (.node) and the distro node
                            launchers that load libnode

  Bun is not detected and not excluded: Bun-compiled executables match only
  Node_Binary_Broad (an accepted false positive, reported with no version).

  No modules are imported so the rules also work in embedded YARA engines
  (osquery, EDRs) that are built without the pe/elf/macho modules.

  See README.md for tested samples and the ABI number -> Node major table.
*/

// Condition copied from is_executable.yar by sync_rules.py - edit it there
private rule Node_Detect_IsExecutable
{{
  condition:
    // ELF executable (2) or shared object (3, also PIE executables); e_type is
    // in the byte order given by EI_DATA (1 = little, 2 = big endian)
    (uint32(0) == 0x464C457F and
      ((uint8(5) == 1 and (uint16(16) == 2 or uint16(16) == 3)) or
       (uint8(5) == 2 and (uint16be(16) == 2 or uint16be(16) == 3))))
    // PE: MZ header whose e_lfanew (0x3C) points at "PE\0\0"
    or (uint16(0) == 0x5A4D and uint32(uint32(0x3C)) == 0x00004550)
    // Mach-O 32/64 execute (2), dylib (6) or bundle (8, e.g. PHP extensions)
    or ((uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
        (uint32(12) == 2 or uint32(12) == 6 or uint32(12) == 8))
    // same, byte-swapped (big-endian) Mach-O
    or ((uint32(0) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(0) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
        (uint32be(12) == 2 or uint32be(12) == 6 or uint32be(12) == 8))
    // Mach-O universal (CAFEBABE) with 1-19 architectures whose first slice
    // passes the thin Mach-O check above, so universal static libraries (.a),
    // object files and dSYMs are rejected. Java .class files also start with
    // CAFEBABE, but bytes 4-7 hold their class version (major >= 45), not an
    // architecture count. The header is big-endian; the first slice's offset
    // is at 16 (fat_arch.offset).
    or (uint32(0) == 0xBEBAFECA and uint32be(4) > 0 and uint32be(4) < 20 and
        (((uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
          (uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 2 or uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 8)) or
         ((uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
          (uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 2 or uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 8))))
    // same for the rare 64-bit universal header (CAFEBABF): fat_arch_64.offset
    // is 8 bytes at 16; slices sit well below 4 GB, so its low half (20) is used
    or (uint32(0) == 0xBFBAFECA and uint32be(4) > 0 and uint32be(4) < 20 and
        (((uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
          (uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 2 or uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 8)) or
         ((uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
          (uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 2 or uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 8))))
}

rule Node_Runtime_Version
{{
  meta:
    description = "Node.js runtime (node, node.exe, libnode, or a runtime embedding Node: Electron, SEA, pkg); $ver = exact Node version"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // Inspector /json/version "Browser" value: "node.js/" NODE_VERSION. In
    // every official build 8.17.0-25.9.0, distro libnode, Electron and SEA.
    // A suffix only after "-" (-rc.1, -nightly...): the compiler can merge the
    // literal with the next string (linux-x64 24.22.1: "v24.22.1Protocol-...")
    $ver = /node\.js\/v[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}\.[0-9]{{1,3}(-[0-9A-Za-z.]{{1,20})?/
    // process.release.sourceUrl / headersUrl. Also in Bun (Node compatibility),
    // so it only counts together with the NODE_MODULE ABI symbol, which Bun
    // lacks; needed for vercel/pkg builds, which have no inspector string.
    // No "not Bun" exclusion: it could hide a real Node binary whose embedded
    // JavaScript mentions Bun.
    $rel = /https:\/\/nodejs\.org\/download\/release\/v[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}\.[0-9]{{1,3}/
    // NODE_MODULE registration symbol, ABI = NODE_MODULE_VERSION (10.x and later)
    $abi = /node_register_module_v[0-9]{{2,3}/
  condition:
    Node_Detect_IsExecutable and ($ver or ($rel and $abi))
}

rule Node_Electron_Version
{{
  meta:
    description = "Electron framework (embeds Node.js); $electron = Electron version, $ver = embedded Node version"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // Electron user agent. Both keep a "-" suffix (31.0.0-nightly.20240101), the
    // same as Node_Runtime_Version's $ver, so one file gives one node version
    $electron = /Electron\/[0-9]{{1,3}\.[0-9]{{1,3}\.[0-9]{{1,3}(-[0-9A-Za-z.]{{1,20})?/
    $ver = /node\.js\/v[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}\.[0-9]{{1,3}(-[0-9A-Za-z.]{{1,20})?/
    // Old Electron (2.x) has no node.js/v, only the NODE_MODULE registration
    // function; it is then reported by its Electron version alone
    $reg = "node_module_register"
  condition:
    Node_Detect_IsExecutable and $electron and ($ver or $reg)
}

rule Node_Binary_Broad
{{
  meta:
    description = "Broad catch-all: Node runtime, libnode launcher, or native addon (.node)"
    confidence = "medium"
  strings:
    $ver    = "node.js/v"
    $rel    = "https://nodejs.org/download/release/v"
    $abi    = /node_register_module_v[0-9]{{2,3}/   // NODE_MODULE ABI, also in addons
    $napi   = "napi_register_module_v1"              // N-API addon export
    $napiim = "napi_module_register"                 // N-API addon import
    $start  = "_ZN4node5StartEiPPc"                  // distro launcher importing node::Start from libnode
    $reg    = "node_module_register"                 // NODE_MODULE: legacy (non-N-API) addons, old runtimes
  condition:
    // Also matches Bun-compiled executables (release URL, N-API): an accepted
    // false positive, reported as "node unknown"
    Node_Detect_IsExecutable and any of them
}
_END_OF_RULE_
delete "{parameter "signatures_folder"}{parameter "sep"}node_detect.yar"
move __createfile "{parameter "signatures_folder"}{parameter "sep"}node_detect.yar"

// apache_detect.yar
delete __createfile
createfile until _END_OF_RULE_
/*
  Apache HTTP Server (httpd) + mod_http2 detection + version, all OSes (Linux
  ELF, Windows PE, macOS Mach-O).

  Signatures based on jeffschafer's Apache mod_http2 scanner. Run with
  `yara -s` (or `yr scan -s`) to print the matched version text.

  Rules:
    Apache_HTTPD_Version - the file holding the httpd core: httpd on Linux and
                           macOS, libhttpd.dll on Windows (httpd.exe is a small
                           launcher); $ver holds the exact version (Apache/2.4.67)
    Apache_HTTP2_Module  - mod_http2 (mod_http2.so, or httpd with it built in);
                           $_module_ver is a candidate module version only

  No modules are imported so the rules also work in embedded YARA engines
  (osquery, EDRs) that are built without the pe/elf/macho modules.
*/

// Condition copied from is_executable.yar by sync_rules.py - edit it there
private rule Apache_Detect_IsExecutable
{{
  condition:
    // ELF executable (2) or shared object (3, also PIE executables); e_type is
    // in the byte order given by EI_DATA (1 = little, 2 = big endian)
    (uint32(0) == 0x464C457F and
      ((uint8(5) == 1 and (uint16(16) == 2 or uint16(16) == 3)) or
       (uint8(5) == 2 and (uint16be(16) == 2 or uint16be(16) == 3))))
    // PE: MZ header whose e_lfanew (0x3C) points at "PE\0\0"
    or (uint16(0) == 0x5A4D and uint32(uint32(0x3C)) == 0x00004550)
    // Mach-O 32/64 execute (2), dylib (6) or bundle (8, e.g. PHP extensions)
    or ((uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
        (uint32(12) == 2 or uint32(12) == 6 or uint32(12) == 8))
    // same, byte-swapped (big-endian) Mach-O
    or ((uint32(0) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(0) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
        (uint32be(12) == 2 or uint32be(12) == 6 or uint32be(12) == 8))
    // Mach-O universal (CAFEBABE) with 1-19 architectures whose first slice
    // passes the thin Mach-O check above, so universal static libraries (.a),
    // object files and dSYMs are rejected. Java .class files also start with
    // CAFEBABE, but bytes 4-7 hold their class version (major >= 45), not an
    // architecture count. The header is big-endian; the first slice's offset
    // is at 16 (fat_arch.offset).
    or (uint32(0) == 0xBEBAFECA and uint32be(4) > 0 and uint32be(4) < 20 and
        (((uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
          (uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 2 or uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32(uint32be(16) + 12) == 8)) or
         ((uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(uint32be(16)) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
          (uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 2 or uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32be(uint32be(16) + 12) == 8))))
    // same for the rare 64-bit universal header (CAFEBABF): fat_arch_64.offset
    // is 8 bytes at 16; slices sit well below 4 GB, so its low half (20) is used
    or (uint32(0) == 0xBFBAFECA and uint32be(4) > 0 and uint32be(4) < 20 and
        (((uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xFEEDFACF) and
          (uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 2 or uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32(uint32be(20) + 12) == 8)) or
         ((uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(uint32be(20)) == 0xCFFAEDFE) and
          (uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 2 or uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 6 or
           uint32be(uint32be(20) + 12) == 8))))
}

rule Apache_HTTPD_Version
{{
  meta:
    description = "Apache httpd core (httpd, libhttpd.dll); $ver = server version"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // AP_SERVER_BASEVERSION ("Apache" "/" AP_SERVER_BASEREVISION), one literal
    // in the core. Also in other software (user agent lists, proxies), so it
    // only counts together with a $core marker. Modules built against httpd
    // (mod_ssl, mod_proxy) have it too.
    $ver = /Apache\/2\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}/
    // Only in the core: the directive name from its command table, and its
    // error message when the host name can't be resolved (AH00558 in 2.4).
    // The directive name as a whole C string: mod_security2 has "ServerTokens"
    // in a message, and "ModSecurity for Apache/2.9.7" matches $ver
    $core1 = "\x00ServerTokens\x00"
    $core2 = "Could not reliably determine the server's fully qualified domain name"
  condition:
    Apache_Detect_IsExecutable and $ver and any of ($core*)
}

rule Apache_HTTP2_Module
{{
  meta:
    description = "Apache mod_http2; $_module_ver = candidate module version"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // Not "http2_module": it is also inside mod_proxy_http2's proxy_http2_module
    $module_identity = "mod_http2_init_counter"
    $module_log = "mod_http2 (v%s, feats="
    // MOD_HTTP2_VERSION as a bare C string, reported as the mod_http2 version.
    // Candidate evidence only: any bare "2.x.y" string matches, and the same
    // mod_http2 version ships with several httpd releases. Optional - the
    // leading "_" lets it go unused in the condition while `-s` still prints it.
    // A suffix only after "-": RHEL's separate mod_http2 package has "2.0.26-git"
    $_module_ver = /\x002\.[0-9]\.[0-9]{{1,3}(-[0-9A-Za-z.]{{1,20})?\x00/
  condition:
    Apache_Detect_IsExecutable and
    ($module_identity or $module_log)
}
_END_OF_RULE_
delete "{parameter "signatures_folder"}{parameter "sep"}apache_detect.yar"
move __createfile "{parameter "signatures_folder"}{parameter "sep"}apache_detect.yar"

// java_detect.yar
delete __createfile
createfile until _END_OF_RULE_
rule Java_Version_And_Vendor_Detector
{{
    meta:
        description = "Detects and reports Java/JDK version and distribution vendor"
        author = "Security Analyst"

    strings:
        // 1. Version strings, modern 9+ and legacy 1.6-1.8 in one pattern.
        // Named $ver because the scan tasks' summariser only reads a version
        // from $ver, $pv, $rel, $electron or $_module_ver; under any other name
        // the match is reported with version "unknown".
        // JAVA_VERSION is the on-disk spelling used in the JDK "release" file;
        // java.runtime.version is the runtime system property. Without the
        // uppercase form a modern JDK is not detected: its release file carries
        // the version but never the lowercase spelling.
        // JAVA_RUNTIME_VERSION is deliberately NOT listed. It matches in
        // addition to JAVA_VERSION, so every install would report twice, and its
        // value is cut at the first dot of a distro suffix - Ubuntu's
        // 11.0.33+9-post-1ubuntu1-22.04.1-Ubuntu came out as ...-1ubuntu1-22.
        // JAVA_VERSION is always the plain X.Y.Z or 1.8.0_nnn form.
        //
        // The trailing "JRE 1.x.0" branch is for runtimes that ship no release
        // file at all - IBM Semeru / OpenJ9 JREs of the Java 8 era. There the
        // only version evidence is a banner template compiled into j9vmNN.dll,
        // so this reports the Java LEVEL (1.8.0) and never the update level:
        // the runtime fills the update in at execution time. Two rows per
        // install are expected, because OpenJ9 ships the same VM twice, under
        // bin/default and bin/compressedrefs. Treat a hit as "this runtime is
        // present, inspect it by hand for the patch level".
        // It carries no keyword of its own, so it leans on the vendor half of
        // the condition to avoid matching a bare version string anywhere.
        $ver = /(openjdk|java\.runtime\.version|JAVA_VERSION|Java\(TM\) SE Runtime Environment)[=:\s"]+((9|[12][0-9])\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+([+._-][0-9A-Za-z-]+)?|1\.[6-8]\.0_[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z-]+)?)|JRE 1\.[6-8]\.0/ ascii wide

        // 2. Explicit Vendor Properties (found in binaries, memory, and JDK 'release' files)
        // BUILD_TYPE is here because Oracle 6/7/8 release files carry no vendor
        // key at all - no IMPLEMENTOR, no java.vendor, no "Oracle Corporation" -
        // so the version matches but nothing satisfies the vendor half and the
        // install goes undetected. BUILD_TYPE="commercial" is an Oracle build
        // marker and is absent from OpenJDK release files.
        $vendor_prop = /(java\.vendor|java\.vm\.vendor|IMPLEMENTOR|BUILD_TYPE)[=:\s"]+[A-Za-z0-9 ._(),-]{{3,50}/ ascii wide

        // 3. Distribution-Specific Build Signatures
        $vendor_oracle     = "Oracle Corporation" ascii wide
        $vendor_sun        = "Sun Microsystems Inc." ascii wide
        $vendor_temurin    = /Eclipse Adoptium|Temurin-[0-9.+_-]+/ ascii wide
        $vendor_adopt      = /AdoptOpenJDK(-[0-9.+_-]+)?/ ascii wide
        $vendor_corretto   = /Amazon\.com Inc\.|Corretto-[0-9.]+/ ascii wide
        $vendor_zulu       = /Azul Systems|Zulu[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9.+_-]+/ ascii wide
        $vendor_ibm        = /IBM Corporation|IBM J9 VM|Semeru/ ascii wide
        $vendor_microsoft  = /Microsoft-[0-9.+_-]+/ ascii wide
        $vendor_redhat     = "Red Hat, Inc." ascii wide
        $vendor_sap        = /SAP SE|SapMachine/ ascii wide
        $vendor_bellsoft   = /BellSoft|Liberica/ ascii wide

    condition:
        $ver and (
            $vendor_prop or
            any of ($vendor_*)
        )
}
_END_OF_RULE_
delete "{parameter "signatures_folder"}{parameter "sep"}java_detect.yar"
move __createfile "{parameter "signatures_folder"}{parameter "sep"}java_detect.yar"

// Written only after every rule file is in place, so a failed deploy leaves the
// task relevant and the scan tasks running the previous signature set.
delete __createfile
createfile until _END_OF_VERSION_
2026-11-17.5
_END_OF_VERSION_
delete "{parameter "engine_folder"}{parameter "sep"}signatures.version"
move __createfile "{parameter "engine_folder"}{parameter "sep"}signatures.version"
]]></ActionScript>
			<SuccessCriteria Option="RunToCompletion"></SuccessCriteria>
		</DefaultAction>
	</Task>
</BES>
